      "claim": "A music genre is considered “relevant today” when it meets at least two of four industry‑standard metrics: (a) presence in current top‑100 charts or major streaming playlists, (b) high streaming volume (top 10 % of legacy artists), (c) documented influence on contemporary artists, and (d) recent commercial releases in that style that achieve chart success.",
      "evidence": "IFPI Global Music Report 2023 and Nielsen Music use multi‑metric frameworks (chart performance, streaming share, influence surveys) to assess genre vitality; academic studies on music relevance adopt similar criteria.",
